00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.930
In 2005, they came out with
some better nutritional guidance

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.590
and they gave us a pyramid to look at.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.460
What do you take away from it?

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.800
- Oh, there's like different
categories of foods.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.380
- I don't know what I'm
supposed to be saying

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:32.213
right now though.

00:05:32.213 --> 00:05:33.940
- Do they tell you how much
of each food you should eat?

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.890
- No.
- It's confusing. (chuckles)

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.780
It seems like the further he
gets up, the less he eats.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.613
- I don't really get it.

00:05:38.613 --> 00:05:40.320
Get to the top, try to eat all of them.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.770
- This is the steps he
needs to take in his diet

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.873
to reach the top.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:48.803
Nope.

00:05:48.803 --> 00:05:51.330
- Now the good part is My
Pyramid does aim to provide

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.170
some insight into proportionality,

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.670
as represented by these
colorful stripes on the pyramid,

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:56.740
but it stops there,

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.790
leaving you to estimate
how much more orange

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.720
there is than yellow.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.117
It's really, really confusing.

00:06:01.117 --> 00:06:04.760
The chaos of the My Pyramid
wasn't a total waste though,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.890
because there was a wide
variety of foods here,

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.520
unlike the four basic food groups.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.220
There was upwards of 40
different foods on the graphic.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.460
In 2011, the government tossed
all the confusing guidance

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.050
from the pyramid into the trash

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:19.220
and introduced us the
new redesigned My Plate.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.840
It was gonna change how we talked

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.220
and communicated about nutrition.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.630
Unfortunately, they may
have over-corrected.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.970
While the misguided proportions

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:27.270
of the pyramids were now gone,

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.140
they also pulled a complete
180 in regards to fitness.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.490
Where'd the stairs go?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.590
We've also introduced a new
word into our graphic: protein.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.810
And while recognizing that
protein comes in forms

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.510
that extend beyond animal products

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.930
is no doubt an important
evolution in messaging,

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.320
there is but one fatal flaw.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.540
Protein is a macronutrient,
not a food group.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.660
This means that you can
get your protein portion

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.150
with hamburgers and hotdogs.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:52.470
Yeah, tasty, but not an ideal
healthy source of protein.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.060
There is something I love
about My Plate: fish.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.540
For the first time we
actually see guidance

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.600
recommending the consumption of seafood,

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.300
and it's such a healthy food.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.560
It contains omega-3 fatty acids.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.130
We've actually seen evidence
of reductions in heart disease

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.150
and stroke risk.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.280
My biggest issue with
My Plate is that it says

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.570
100% fruit juice is the
equivalent of a fruit serving.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.720
Yeah, maybe the vitamins
and minerals are in there,

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.180
but do you know how much sugar is in here?

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.620
A can of Cola, a popular energy drinks,

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.220
some sugar cubes, fruit juice.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.470
Which one of these four
has the most sugar?

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.270
- I would say the energy drink maybe.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.246
- Probably the can of soda.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.320
- Energy drink.
- Why do you say that?

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.710
- Because I drink energy drink every day

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.020
to do my job. (laughs)

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.390
- And it gives you that sugar kick?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.223
- Yep.

00:07:34.223 --> 00:07:35.056
- Energy drink.
- The soda.

00:07:35.056 --> 00:07:36.260
- What if I was to tell you those two

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.599
have the lowest amount of sugar?

00:07:37.599 --> 00:07:38.760
- [Women] Oh!

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.911
- Probably the pure sugar cubes. No?

00:07:40.911 --> 00:07:41.744
- No.
- No?

00:07:41.744 --> 00:07:42.710
- The fruit juice.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.557
- You're right.
- I am.

00:07:43.557 --> 00:07:45.340
- And I actually sometimes drink it

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.230
thinking that it's more nutrition.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:50.360
- Yes, fruits contain sugar,
but they also contain fiber,

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.270
which slows the absorption of the sugar

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:54.130
thereby not spiking your blood sugar,

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.480
not spiking your insulin.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.870
Drinking 100% fruit juice might get you

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.020
the vitamins and minerals,

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.760
but it's also gonna spike your sugar,

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.530
just like any other
unhealthy sugary beverage.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.320
Folks, just eat the fruit.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:09.020
In strong contrast to the
pasta extravaganza from 1992,

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.690
we finally see vegetables
dominating the plate.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.190
While this is excellent to see,

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.230
the further guidance doesn't differentiate

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.470
between leafy, dark green
vegetables and potatoes.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.350
As much as it breaks my heart to say so,

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.770
potatoes and french fries do not count

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.150
as your daily vegetable.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.010
And that brings us

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.690
to what modern nutritional
guidance is today.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.800
What should you be eating?

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.840
What should I be eating?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.020
For that, we turn to
our friends at Harvard.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:32.853
Back to the kitchen.

00:08:32.853 --> 00:08:34.490
Here's a plate of food recommended

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.130
by Harvard's modern nutritional guidance.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.870
We're entirely removing dairy

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.600
and swapping it out for a
healthy fat like olive oil.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.610
But it's nice that we're
finally making the statement

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.050
that not all fats equal bad

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.110
because there are healthy fats
and they play important roles

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:49.943
within your body.

00:08:49.943 --> 00:08:52.020
Creating hormones, protecting your organs,

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.720
giving you energy, and
even boosting your HDL

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.130
which is your good cholesterol.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.520
For the record, there's nothing
wrong with having dairy.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.510
Remember, we're not
villainizing ingredients.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.460
It's about not having excess dairy

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.370
and not having low quality dairy.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.410
Another great addition
to their recommendations

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.170
is good old-fashioned water.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.640
It's important to stay hydrated,

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:11.560
not only for you to feel healthy,

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.870
but also to encourage your metabolic rate.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.840
Those who are dehydrated actually
have trouble losing weight

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:18.640
and have lower levels of energy.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.473
Also, as you notice,

00:09:19.473 --> 00:09:21.640
the majority of the plate is plant-based,

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:22.620
fruits and vegetables,

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.770
but it's really important to get

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.570
